# Zone arrival card (uses the Chronicle palette)
modules\Arrival.lua

# Welcome Back bookmark (reads the Chronicle, shows once at login)
modules\WelcomeBack.lua

# Welcome dialog: one compact page for a new installation, and /tui about (TwichUI's window look; the automation summary it reads is in WelcomeAutomation.lua)
modules\WelcomeAutomation.lua
modules\Welcome.lua

# New training at level-up (uses the arrival card's look; data from What's Training?, MIT)
modules\TrainingData.lua
modules\Training.lua

# Battle.net friend login card (replaces the game's friend-online pop-up; uses the arrival card's look)
modules\FriendLogin.lua

# Border textures for TwichUI's own frames (plain, LibSharedMedia, EllesmereUI's)
modules\Borders.lua

# Food and Drink buttons (click to eat or drink the best food or drink in your bags), and, optionally,
# their place in EllesmereUI's Unlock Mode (works without EllesmereUI; off until turned on)
modules\FoodDrink.lua
modules\FoodDrinkUnlock.lua
modules\FoodDrinkProbe.lua

# Dungeon Journal on a data bar: an icon that opens or closes the Forever Dungeon Journal (off until turned on; needs
# that addon and a data bar addon that provides LibDataBroker)
modules\DungeonJournalBroker.lua

# Mage spells on a data bar: Mage Travel (teleports and portals) and Mage Conjuring (food and
# water), sharing one menu (uses the Chronicle palette, the arrival card's fonts and the training data)
# and one background and border for it (game textures and LibSharedMedia's; uses modules\Borders.lua)
modules\MenuStyle.lua
modules\SpellMenu.lua
modules\MageTravel.lua
modules\MageConjure.lua

# Mage refreshments: plan conjured food and water for the group, conjure by click or key, and a checklist
# of who has been supplied (Mages, off until turned on; key bindings in Bindings.xml)
modules\Refreshments.lua
modules\RefreshmentsPanel.lua
modules\RefreshmentsShares.lua
modules\RefreshmentsTrade.lua
modules\RefreshmentsBroker.lua

# Mage selling: sells plain, non-conjured food and drink at merchants (Mages, off until turned on, dry run
# first; reads items as modules\FoodDrink.lua does and uses the Chronicle palette for its window)
modules\EllesmereJunk.lua
modules\MageSell.lua
modules\MageSellWindow.lua

# Vendor restocking: keeps chosen items at a target in your bags, bought from merchants that sell them (off until
# turned on; asks before buying unless you confirm otherwise; waits for the selling above to finish first)
modules\Restock.lua
modules\RestockPrompt.lua

# Chat cleaning: hides unwanted messages in the public channels you choose (General, Trade, ...) through the game's
# chat message filters, before any chat frame (or EllesmereUI's chat, which uses the same frames) shows them. Off until
# turned on; whispers, group, guild and system messages are never looked at. Matching is in ChatCleanMatch.lua.
modules\ChatCleanMatch.lua
modules\ChatClean.lua

# Class resource bars: your class's resources as bars (the power the client reports, combo points on the target for
# Rogues and Cat Form Druids, a Druid's mana while shapeshifted), with optional effects. Off until turned on. Resource
# providers know the game, the bar knows how to draw, effects only decorate; the controller owns the events. Uses
# modules\MenuStyle.lua for the background, border, fonts and textures; the settings are in TwichUI_Settings.
classbars\Anim.lua
classbars\Resources.lua
classbars\Config.lua
classbars\Bar.lua
classbars\Effects.lua
classbars\Controller.lua

# RestedXP skin: a TwichUI theme and finish for the RestedXP guide window (off until turned on; uses
# modules\MenuStyle.lua; needs RestedXP, and works without EllesmereUI)
modules\RestedXPSkin.lua

# RestedXP timer bars: the same look on RestedXP's countdown bars (a finish on the skin above; off when it is)
modules\RestedXPTimers.lua

# RestedXP guide on a data bar: click for a menu to turn RestedXP's guide on or off, lock its windows and open its
# guide import (calls RestedXP's own functions; needs RestedXP and a data bar addon that provides LibDataBroker;
# the menu is drawn like the Mage launchers', so it follows modules\SpellMenu.lua and modules\MenuStyle.lua)
modules\RestedXPBrokerMenu.lua
modules\RestedXPBroker.lua

# SpeakStone skin: a TwichUI look for SpeakStone's speech frame (off until turned on; uses
# modules\MenuStyle.lua; needs SpeakStone, and works without EllesmereUI)
modules\SpeakStoneSkin.lua

# Party pins: named map pins of your own, and ones shared with party members who have TwichUI (on by default,
# can be turned off; their own addon prefix, never chat; uses the Chronicle palette, modules\MenuStyle.lua and setup\Share.lua's names)
# Map pings (Ping.lua, PingMap.lua): a spot on the world map shared with your group for a few seconds, with a recent list
# at the top right of the map. Part of Party pins, with its own prefix; Ping.lua has no frames, PingMap.lua draws them.
# Map tools (MapTools.lua): a small bar on the world map with the pin and ping shortcuts as buttons, through the same helpers.
pins\Pins.lua
pins\Sync.lua
pins\Look.lua
pins\Map.lua
pins\Minimap.lua
pins\Editor.lua
pins\Window.lua
pins\Way.lua
pins\Sound.lua
pins\Ping.lua
pins\PingMap.lua
pins\MapTools.lua
pins\BrokerMenu.lua
pins\Broker.lua

# Navigation: a walking route to a place you choose (a pin's Navigate here, the map tool, /tui nav), planned over walking
# maps baked from the client's terrain (TwichUI_NavData, load on demand, loaded the first time a route is planned; tools/navbake
# has how they are made). A frame, a direction arrow, and the route on the world map and the minimap. Off until turned on;
# nothing runs while no destination is set. Data.lua and Route.lua have no frames.
nav\Prefs.lua
nav\Data.lua
nav\Route.lua
nav\Journey.lua
nav\Nav.lua
nav\Travel.lua
nav\Paint.lua
nav\Unlock.lua
nav\Frame.lua
nav\Arrow.lua
nav\MapTrail.lua
nav\MinimapTrail.lua

# World map exploration: one seamless world map. Every continent's and zone's painting (the game's own textures) stitched
# onto the world map, so the wheel zooms from the whole world into any zone, city or cave and back; the map underneath
# follows what you look at. Terrain detail up close, caves' maps surfacing, dungeons' maps, and dungeon, cave and boat or
# zeppelin places that take you where they lead. Off until turned on, and off while OpenMap is loaded. Data.lua (made by
# tools/mapdata from the game clients) holds texture file IDs and places, no art. Prefs, ViewMath and World have no
# frames; View.lua owns the view and is the only part moving it; Art.lua draws the stitched painting.
map\Prefs.lua
map\Data.lua
map\ViewMath.lua
map\World.lua
map\View.lua
map\Art.lua
map\Detail.lua
map\Controls.lua
map\Caves.lua
map\Places.lua
map\DungeonView.lua

# Vendors and trainers: the NPCs you deal with (merchants by what they sell, trainers, bankers, innkeepers and other
# services), noted where you stood and shown on the world map by the kinds you choose; your list can be sent to another
# TwichUI user, your group or your guild when you choose, and theirs taken in as reports (asks first). Off until turned
# on; nothing listens while it is off. Kinds.lua decides what an NPC is (no game calls), Store.lua keeps the list,
# Collect.lua reads the game's windows, Map.lua draws (through pins\Map.lua's placing), Share.lua sends and receives.
npcs\Kinds.lua
npcs\Store.lua
npcs\Prefs.lua
npcs\Collect.lua
npcs\Map.lua
npcs\Share.lua
npcs\Knowledge.lua

# Cozy Sleeping Bag guide: a small window that follows the hidden quest chain behind the bag, from the character's own quest
# history (nothing saved but where the window sits), with optional map pins made through pins\Pins.lua. Never opens by itself;
# nothing listens while it is closed. Data and State have no frames or game calls; CozyBag.lua reads the game; the window draws.
guides\CozyBagData.lua
guides\CozyBagState.lua
guides\CozyBag.lua
guides\CozyBagWindow.lua

# Hunter ammunition warning: a line of text near the centre of the screen when a Hunter's ammunition is missing, out or the
# wrong kind for the ranged weapon (Hunters only, off until turned on; nothing is equipped, moved or bought for you).
# Config.lua is what it stores, Items.lua what counts as ammunition (and the player's own list), State.lua the judgement
# (no game calls), Warning.lua the events and the frame. Uses modules\MenuStyle.lua for the font and the optional panel;
# the settings are in TwichUI_Settings.
ammo\Config.lua
ammo\Items.lua
ammo\State.lua
ammo\Warning.lua

# Hazard alerts: a sound for each of three alert categories when an aura you list lands on you, grows or fades, played by the
# game itself through its aura-sound registration (the client gives addons no combat-log payload, so no damage is read).
# Off until turned on; nothing runs when a hazard happens. Config.lua is what it stores, Rules.lua what is registered (no game
# calls), Alerts.lua the registration and the preview sound. The settings are in TwichUI_Settings.
hazard\Config.lua
hazard\Rules.lua
hazard\Alerts.lua

# Sell from Bags: Auction House posting tab (uses the Chronicle palette)
auction\Price.lua
auction\Scan.lua
auction\Window.lua
# Mailbox gold summary: one chat line per mailbox visit (auction\Mail.lua)
auction\Mail.lua

# Quality of Life: small opt-in conveniences (summons, resurrection, release in battlegrounds, duels)
qol\QoL.lua
qol\Summons.lua
qol\Resurrect.lua
qol\ReleasePvP.lua
qol\Duels.lua
qol\QuickKeybind.lua
qol\GuideWaypoint.lua
qol\GuideAutoHide.lua
